From b2f742caf10bf652bec0c64dae107a9124f8efd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rieki777 <rieki@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 14:37:41 -1000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(quest): Phase 3.1 follow-ups (Open Universe reveal +
 animation + hero cards)

Wires the four small follow-ups from QUEST_PAGE_AND_PATH_PROGRESSION_SPEC
sections 4.3, 9.6, 9.7:

* shared/openUniverseReveal.ts (new): seededShuffle + computeReveal
  helpers. Pure functions. Mulberry32 PRNG seeded from a per-player
  hash so every player gets a unique deterministic Open Universe
  unlock order. Reveal split is 2 + completedCount visible, rest
  locked. Used by EpicQuestSection.

* client/src/components/EpicQuestSection.tsx: reads playerProfiles.me
  for the user's questsCompleted list, intersects with EPIC_QUESTS
  ids to count completed Open Universe quests, and runs computeReveal.
  Visible cards render normally; locked cards render as moss-overgrown
  ruins via the LockedQuestCard with an unlockHint and the existing
  per-quest element glyph. Adds a canopy-fall keyframe animation that
  fires once on each visible card per render cycle (single emotional
  beat per spec section 9.7). Pre-Rites players still see all-locked
  silhouettes inside the existing grayscale wrapper.

* client/src/pages/Quest.tsx: hero-card treatment for threshold
  quests (id 0 Fire, 13 Fasting, 14 Food Foresting). Tailwind-only:
  amber ring + soft glow shadow. Spec section 9.6.

No schema changes, no new endpoints. The reveal logic is purely
client-side and reads from existing data sources.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
